        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm identifying the root लजि (भर्त्सने, meaning \"to blame\"), bhvadi parasmaipada, forming लुङ् uttama bahuvacana as लञ्जामः, and double-checking the dhatupatha classification for this root.\n\nBut working through the sic-luṅ derivation, I realize the vṛddhi rule अतो हलादेर्लघोः requires the अ to be laghu, which it isn't here since ञ्ज् makes it guru — so अलाञ्जिष्म seems questionable unless the actual root is लाजि (with long आ) rather than लजि, since the dhatupatha separately lists \"लाज लाजि भर्जने च\" alongside \"लज लजि भर्त्सने.\"\n\nWith लाजि as the root, लाञ्ज् gives luṅ अलाञ्जीत्, and the first-person plural अलाञ्जिष्म, making present तत् लाञ्जामः the answer.\n\n",
